He clicked on "1970, China."

A flash of white light swept through, engulfing the surrounding space.

When he opened his eyes again, he found himself in a warmly lit room. The furnishings around him were very antiquated, yet strangely interspersed with a few modern items.

A 1970s school classroom . A red banner hung on the wall read: "Warmly celebrate the start of the new 1970 school semester." The teacher was lecturing in front of the blackboard, while the students, dressed in old-style blue uniforms, were all looking down and playing with their smartphones. Outside the window, both the sun and the moon were visible in the sky.

After class, Xiaolin walked onto the street . The street was lined with old-fashioned signs reading "Barbershop" and "Restaurant." Pedestrians were dressed in gray-blue Zhongshan suits, yet some were looking down at their phones. A drone flew overhead, capturing the street scene. Parked by the roadside was not an old-fashioned bicycle, but a sports car.

At the street corner, he entered the "People's Store" . The store shelves were neatly arranged, and a prominent red banner on the wall was marked "1976." The cashier was using a computer to check out customers, while a male customer nearby was examining a smartwatch. A child holding a drink asked, "Uncle, why are your clothes so strange?"

Then Xiaolin approached the factory entrance and noticed workers bustling with mechanized production inside. All the machinery appeared antiquated, yet a robot suddenly appeared among them. With your keen eyes, can you spot any other anachronistic details that seem out of place?
